<title>USA: World Bank chief backs Venezuela's reforms.</title>
<headline>World Bank chief backs Venezuela's reforms.</headline>
<text>
<p>WASHINGTON, Sept 27 (Reuter - World Bank President James Wolfensohn backed Venezuela's economic reform efforts Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;We believe the programs are sensible,&quot; he told a news conference. &quot;The situation has stabilized. Things are in better shape in Venezuela.&quot;</p>
<p>Nevertheless, he said he expects the country to continue to borrow money from the World Bank for some time to come.</p>
</text>
